WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.145
A refrigerator moves heat out of the food compartment.

2
00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:06.405
A fluid called refrigerant flows through these inside coils.

3
00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.885
As it boils into gas,

4
00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:09.770
it absorbs heat from the air and food.

5
00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:12.145
The compressor squeezes the gas,

6
00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.105
raising its pressure and temperature.

7
00:00:14.105 --> 00:00:16.605
It then flows through the outside coils.

8
00:00:16.605 --> 00:00:18.425
Here it releases heat into the room

9
00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:20.225
and turns back into liquid.

10
00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:22.370
That’s why a fridge can feel warm at the back.

11
00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:25.525
Next, the liquid passes through a narrow valve.

12
00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.745
Its pressure drops,

13
00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:29.565
and some of it evaporates, making a cold mixture.

14
00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:31.665
That flows back through the inside coils

15
00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:33.365
to absorb more heat.

16
00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.970
The same fluid goes around again.
